From 9502adfa1d77184e5442bf41e2e6a078aab4221d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "MOTOR-46 (Claude)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:59:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] sync: FlyWeb 3.2 sync account client service (H3)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FlyWeb/docs/sync-cuenta.md §5, §6, §8, §9 and §11, with the decisions of
§10.1 and the protocol of FlyWeb/servidor/sync/cuenta (softmac PR #977).

flyweb_sync::AccountService, one per regular profile, created with it:

- talks to /cuenta/v1 on the origin of --sync-url (HTTPS, or HTTP on
  loopback for a test instance), JSON only, no cookies, 30 s per call, the
  chain proof in the X-FlyWeb-* headers after a one-use nonce, the device
  token as Authorization: Bearer;
- the account id, email, device id, token and last event read are prefs
  encrypted with OSCrypt like the seed; one that does not decrypt gives the
  «claves ilegibles» state;
- the password is stretched off the UI thread, one at a time, and wiped;
  KL/KU only stay in memory between the two steps of «entrar» and «cambiar
  el email», up to the 10 minutes of the code;
- create (linking this Mac's chain, or a new one), log in with email +
  password + code (the wrap must open, P15), join with the 24 words (or 25
  with a valid date), change the password with a code, change the email,
  change the sync key (new seed, both proofs, leave and rejoin), devices
  (list, remove, rename), «No he sido yo», delete everywhere, cancel a
  scheduled deletion, leave on this Mac, and the mailbox-only deletion and
  «Empezar de cero»;
- polls the account events every 15 minutes while sync is on (backing off
  up to 1 h), renews an invalidated token with the chain proof, registers a
  Mac that joined with the words (decision 11), skips the account history
  on the first poll and the events of its own operations, and turns a chain
  disabled from elsewhere into «cuenta borrada» or «clave cambiada» by
  asking the server with the old keys, still in memory.

It does not touch the sync engine, Nigori or BraveSyncAuthManager: it joins
and leaves chains through BraveSyncServiceImpl's public calls.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
